  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PARASITES IN BWINDI GREAT APES: ECOLOGY, EPIDEMIOLOGY AND HEALTH IMPACTS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CHARACTERIZE PARASITE COMMUNITIES IN GREAT APES AND DRIVING FACTORS OF A FATAL CHRONIC WASTING SYNDROME AFFECTING CRITICALLY ENDANGERED MOUNTAIN GORILLAS AND ENDANGERED EASTERN CHIMPANZEES IN BWINDI IMPENETRABLE NATIONAL PARK, UGANDA BY: (1) DETERMINING THE PARASITE DIVERSITY AND INFECTION BURDEN IN THE PARK S GREAT APES (2) DETECTING POSSIBLE RESERVOIRS OF ZOONOTIC PARASITES AFFECTING THE PARK S WILDLIFE (3) EVALUATING THE ROLE OF STRONGYLID PARASITES IN THE CLINICAL SYNDROME (4) INVESTIGATING FORCES DRIVING ZOONOTIC PARASITE INFECTIONS IN GREAT APES (5) INCREASING THE CAPACITY OF THE DISEASE SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM AND (6) INCREASING LOCAL COMMUNITIES AWARENESS OF PATHOGEN TRANSMISSION RISKS.</narrative>
  </description>
